ap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\b1 \fs36 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \ul1 Finding Routes}{\fs22 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang9 \langnp9 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang9 \langnp9 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 Introduction:}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang9 \langnp9 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052  }{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 The "Find Route" algorithm evaluates possible routes between a Start and End location. It considers both the travel time and travel cost of alternate routes. The "Secs/Silver" value specifies the exchange rate between time and money, i.e., the default value of 10 says that you would be willing to travel an extra 10 seconds to save 1 silver in cost. Higher values (max 99) will prefer lower cost routes that will take longer. Lower values (min 1) will prefer faster routes at a higher cost. The algorithm will then pick the most effective route based on this criteria. Be sure to set the factions that you have Friend reputation with in the Travel Discounts window so that the cost calculations will be accurate.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 Warning:}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052  You must set the appropriate travel requirement selections for each character (use the Requirements button) so that the plugin knows which travel destinations are available to your character. You may also need to use the "Not Visited" flag to disable stables that you haven't discovered yet. Read the Requirements file for a detailed explanation of each of the requirement settings.}{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang9 \langnp9 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 Start and End selection}{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang9 \langnp9 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 :}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang9 \langnp9 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052  }{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 The basic way to find a route is to first set the starting location by selecting the Zone and then the stable Location within the zone followed by clicking on the Set Start button. You can automatically find the nearest stable by clicking on the "Find nearest Stable" button (you still need to click Set Start). Once the Start location has been set, you can evaluate one or more destinations.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 You then select the desired destination Zone and Location and click on the Find Route button to find the best route. The displayed route will show the total travel time and cost and each step in the route. An "(ST)" suffix indicates a Swift Travel route and a "(MT)" suffix indicates a Manual Travel route (i.e., you use your own horse.) You can then set an alternate destination and do another Find route. A few MT routes are included to link destinations that would otherwise be unreachable or require a very long detour.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 Instead of using a single start location with alternate destinations, you can set a single End location and consider multiple Start locations. This is done by clicking the check box next to the "Set Start" button, changing it into a "Set End" button. You then select the end Zone and Location and click on the Set End button to save the location. Now you can choose different Start locations (including using the "Find nearest Stable" button) and click on the Find Route button to find the best route using that starting location. This process can be automated by using the "Find best Start" button as described in the next section.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 Find best Start:}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052  If you want to take advantage of milestones, Return to skills}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 ,}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052  class skills (Guide to/Muster in),}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052  and Travel to House skills}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052  you can use the "Find best Start" feature, but first you have to configure these abilities for each character.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 Currently known milestones are set by first selecting the Zone and Location, then selecting the milestone number (up to 8 can be set) and finally clicking on the "Set Milestone Location" button. This should be done for each milestone in use. You can check your current milestone settings with the command "/tr ms". If you set a new milestone, be sure to also set it in this plugin.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 Currently known "Return to" destinations can be set by opening the window with the "/trw rt" command and clicking on the check box for each known destination. The plugin will use the racial version of the destination as appropriate for your race. To display reputation based destinations that could be learned, use the command "/tr rt" and cursor over the links to see the requirements (Ost Guruth is a special case with no linkable object). When you learn a new destination, be sure to add it to the settings.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 If you are a Hunter or Warden, you can also set class based destinations by opening the window with the "/trw gm" command and clicking on the check box for each known destination. The plugin will use the destination list appropriate for your class. To see where these skills can be learned and what the requirements are, you can use my Camp Site reference plugin.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 If you have a stable at your house or can easily access one from your house, you can include it in the route search. Use the Set House Travel button (or enter \uc1 \u8216 ?/trw ht\uc1 \u8217 ?) to open the the House Travel settings window. Select which of the 4 house travel skills is best for you (selecting <none> will disable it) and then enter the time it takes you to travel from your house recall position to the desired stable manager. Then click the Save Settings button to commit the change.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 Once all the travel skills have been set, you can then proceed as follows: First set the destination (change Set Start to Set End, select the destination and click on Set End), then use the "Find nearest Stable" button to select the closest stable (you can skip this step if not near a stable) and then click on the "Find best Start" button.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 If the destination is one that you have a travel skill for, the icon the the skill will be displayed as soon as you set the destination and all you need to do is click on the icon to travel. If not, you current location and each of your travel skill locations will be evaluated as possible start locations and the most effective one will be chosen based travel time and cost. If a skill location is chosen, the skill icon will be displayed and you can click on it to start your route.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 Note:}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052  By using the "Set End" feature you can avoid the need to include travel skills on your action bars as the appropriate skill can be selected this way.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052  You can make }{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 "Set End" }{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 the default by enabling it in the Options panel of the Plugin Manager.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \nowidctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \par }}